WEBVTT

00:00:00.455 --> 00:00:05.930
Your business holds Bitcoin but needs working capital With Tillward you borrow

00:00:05.955 --> 00:00:09.394
against that Bitcoin and repay from customer receipts

00:00:10.442 --> 00:00:15.535
Create a business account and borrow MUSD through Mezo Here two thousand

00:00:15.561 --> 00:00:20.093
test MUSD is backed by zero point zero four five test Bitcoin

00:00:25.455 --> 00:00:29.026
You choose how much of each customer payment goes toward the loan

00:00:29.297 --> 00:00:33.088
Set a cash floor too so the business keeps money available for

00:00:33.113 --> 00:00:34.552
everyday expenses

00:00:39.442 --> 00:00:43.614
Create an invoice and share the payment link Your customer approves the

00:00:43.639 --> 00:00:49.285
exact MUSD amount then pays The receipt and its repayment allocation are

00:00:49.311 --> 00:00:51.290
recorded in your business account

00:00:54.442 --> 00:00:59.105
Take a five hundred MUSD payment with a twenty percent repayment rule

00:00:59.389 --> 00:01:04.877
One hundred goes toward the loan Four hundred stays for operations Repayment

00:01:04.903 --> 00:01:07.763
checks your cash floor and Mezo's minimum debt

00:01:09.455 --> 00:01:14.141
Here's that flow on public testnet A separate customer wallet paid five

00:01:14.166 --> 00:01:19.536
hundred MUSD One hundred reduced the Mezo loan Later payments brought the

00:01:19.561 --> 00:01:23.496
totals to five hundred and two collected and one hundred point four

00:01:23.521 --> 00:01:24.329
repaid

00:01:26.442 --> 00:01:29.654
Top up the account when you're ready to close the loan We

00:01:29.679 --> 00:01:34.101
tested that through Rabby The debt reached zero and all zero point

00:01:34.126 --> 00:01:37.237
zero four five test Bitcoin returned to the owner

00:01:41.455 --> 00:01:46.881
The public demo includes onboarding invoices and repayment across three test accounts

00:01:47.153 --> 00:01:52.720
Next we'll test demand with businesses willing to collect MUSD Test assets

00:01:52.745 --> 00:01:53.382
only

00:01:54.442 --> 00:01:59.145
Try Tillward Follow the receipts and explore the code on GitHub
